<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qut</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qut is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-turkic">Old Turkic</a> concept of heavenly charisma or good fortune, believed to be granted by the sky god Tengri to a legitimate ruler. Possession of qut justified a qaghan's authority over the steppe peoples. It was a central element of the political ideology of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gokturk-khaganate">Gokturk Empire</a>, expressed in texts such as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orkhon-inscriptions">Orkhon inscriptions</a>.</p></div>
